{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24782 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Melitensin is implicated in the interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Melitensin directly targets NCI-H727, which is a compound that in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, Melitensin is also shown to target CD70 antigen, which is further targeted by another compound, (4R,6R)-3,4,6-trihydroxy-2-methylcyclohex-2-en-1-one, which also targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that Melitensin may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple pathways, possibly by modulating the activity of different molecular targets. The integration of these pathways suggests that Melitensin may exert its effects by influencing the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C through various molecular intermediates, highlighting a complex but interconnected mechanism.",
